      "body": "## Motivation\n\nThe Mistral tool parser deletes `]` from ordinary streamed replies, corrupting code such as `items[0]` and Markdown links. Fixes #44219.\n\n## Modifications\n\nPreserve ordinary text. Consume one closing bracket only when ending a real tool-call array. Add regressions for split text and both Mistral tool formats.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\n37 parser tests and 6 subtests passed. The 6 new regression cases fail on the original code and pass with this fix. No model weights or accelerator needed.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nOnly text parsing changes; no model or kernel changes. No inference benchmark was run.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Pre-commit passed (Rust-only hooks skipped; no Rust changes).\n- [x] Added and ran regression tests.\n- [x] No documentation change needed for this bug fix.\n- [x] Included validation results; inference accuracy/speed tests do not apply.\n- [x] Followed SGLang code style.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #38525883956](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38525883956)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #38525884010](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38525884010)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #38525884632](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38525884632)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
